1
00:00:33,060 --> 00:00:36,829
"All men are potential perpetrators."

2
00:00:36,854 --> 00:00:38,702
(All men are potential perpetrators.)

3
00:00:44,438 --> 00:00:45,972
Agree, two.

4
00:00:46,507 --> 00:00:48,074
Disagree, ten.

5
00:00:52,513 --> 00:00:55,482
They really just hit you with a topic
out of nowhere like this.

6
00:00:55,717 --> 00:00:56,935
The moment the topic dropped,

7
00:00:56,959 --> 00:00:59,486
there was a noticeable stir
among the cast.

8
00:00:59,487 --> 00:01:01,488
It felt like the calm before the storm.

9
00:01:03,023 --> 00:01:06,058
I hope this helps everyone
understand each other a bit better.

10
00:01:13,834 --> 00:01:16,002
The silence hanging between us...

11
00:01:16,237 --> 00:01:17,571
There was an awkward tension.

12
00:01:20,775 --> 00:01:21,775
Two votes.

13
00:01:22,376 --> 00:01:23,476
Against ten.

14
00:01:25,212 --> 00:01:28,147
Two people actually agreed with that?

15
00:01:28,416 --> 00:01:32,486
My guess is the two who agreed were women.

16
00:01:32,487 --> 00:01:35,456
These days, you even hear about cases...

17
00:01:35,457 --> 00:01:40,995
where girls deliberately frame boys
as perpetrators.

18
00:01:40,996 --> 00:01:42,029
Don't you watch the news?

19
00:01:42,030 --> 00:01:45,532
There are plenty of stories about husbands
getting beaten by their wives too.

20
00:01:45,833 --> 00:01:48,502
She might have actually experienced
violence from a man before.

21
00:01:48,503 --> 00:01:50,670
I don't know her past.

22
00:01:50,671 --> 00:01:53,138
Still, I hope she hasn't completely
lost faith in people.

23
00:01:53,139 --> 00:01:55,375
Not all men are potential perpetrators.

24
00:01:55,869 --> 00:02:02,041
I didn't get the sense that anyone here
was genuinely anti-men.

25
00:02:02,383 --> 00:02:03,884
So this came as a real surprise.

26
00:02:04,819 --> 00:02:06,619
I guess this is tonight's
discussion topic.

27
00:02:07,972 --> 00:02:09,455
I never saw that coming.

28
00:02:10,591 --> 00:02:12,859
Looks like they're going to give us
a topic like this every day.

29
00:02:21,101 --> 00:02:24,003
The second the topic came up,
the whole room went dead silent.

30
00:02:24,338 --> 00:02:27,740
It's not exactly typical
dinner-table conversation.

31
00:02:27,741 --> 00:02:28,575
True.

32
00:02:31,412 --> 00:02:32,888
I am curious about one thing, though.

33
00:02:32,913 --> 00:02:36,783
Do you think any of the guys
might have voted yes...

34
00:02:36,784 --> 00:02:38,785
to "All men are potential perpetrators"?

35
00:02:43,858 --> 00:02:44,925
They might have.

36
00:02:44,926 --> 00:02:46,327
- I think so.
- It's possible.

37
00:02:46,328 --> 00:02:47,160
Definitely possible.

38
00:02:47,161 --> 00:02:48,195
Of course it's possible.

39
00:02:49,396 --> 00:02:50,563
Entirely possible.

40
00:02:50,564 --> 00:02:52,365
Everyone sees things differently.

41
00:02:53,033 --> 00:02:55,134
But at two out of twelve,

42
00:02:55,535 --> 00:02:57,870
don't you think they're more
likely to be women?

43
00:02:57,871 --> 00:02:59,205
- Especially those two.
- Sure, it's possible.

44
00:02:59,206 --> 00:03:00,743
Strictly speaking,
in terms of probability.

45
00:03:00,768 --> 00:03:01,842
Right, statistically speaking.

46
00:03:02,370 --> 00:03:02,870
Yes.

47
00:03:04,144 --> 00:03:06,078
If I had to guess,

48
00:03:06,079 --> 00:03:08,214
I'd say they probably hold
a somewhat negative view of men.

49
00:03:08,215 --> 00:03:10,583
Which makes it pretty likely
they're women.

50
00:03:10,751 --> 00:03:13,953
Either they've had
bad experiences with men,

51
00:03:14,088 --> 00:03:15,155
or on the flip side,

52
00:03:15,790 --> 00:03:18,024
they tend to view themselves...

53
00:03:18,636 --> 00:03:19,892
as more dominant than men.

54
00:03:19,893 --> 00:03:23,630
My first guesses would be
Polar Bear and Go Ae Shin.

55
00:03:23,831 --> 00:03:25,365
One thing they have in common...

56
00:03:25,599 --> 00:03:28,868
is that they're both very assertive
whenever they talk to the guys.

57
00:03:29,003 --> 00:03:32,706
I also noticed their expressions...

58
00:03:32,707 --> 00:03:34,975
and body language can feel
a bit confrontational,

59
00:03:34,976 --> 00:03:38,477
making them stand out
as much bolder than the others.

60
00:03:38,478 --> 00:03:40,679
The second Nangja heard the prompt,
she went,

61
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:44,316
"If you're a guy,
wouldn't you naturally..."

62
00:03:44,785 --> 00:03:48,888
"have no choice but to vote no?"

63
00:03:49,189 --> 00:03:50,266
From the way she reacted,

64
00:03:50,290 --> 00:03:52,064
I suspect she's one of the two
who voted yes.

65
00:03:52,593 --> 00:03:55,828
Personally, I voted "no,"

66
00:03:56,297 --> 00:03:59,465
but if you take
"All men are potential perpetrators"...

67
00:03:59,734 --> 00:04:04,504
as a personal attack and think,
"Why are you treating me like a criminal?"

68
00:04:04,505 --> 00:04:06,140
then yeah, no man would ever vote yes.

69
00:04:06,141 --> 00:04:07,547
- She's so well-spoken.
- Like an official spokesperson.

70
00:04:07,572 --> 00:04:08,308
But...

71
00:04:08,610 --> 00:04:14,480
if you step outside
that defensive mindset of,

72
00:04:14,481 --> 00:04:18,350
"Well, I didn't do anything wrong,"

73
00:04:18,619 --> 00:04:23,122
and look at the real-world risks
and violence women face,

74
00:04:23,123 --> 00:04:26,326
I can see how a guy could step back,

75
00:04:26,327 --> 00:04:30,263
look at the bigger picture and think,

76
00:04:30,264 --> 00:04:32,732
"I can understand why women
might see it that way."

77
00:04:32,733 --> 00:04:33,700
Exactly.

78
00:04:35,069 --> 00:04:37,069
Polar Bear definitely gives off
feminist vibes.

79
00:04:37,771 --> 00:04:41,741
At her age,
and with that command of language,

80
00:04:41,742 --> 00:04:43,876
it's almost impossible not to be
a feminist on some level.

81
00:04:43,877 --> 00:04:47,580
To me, feminism is partly about having...

82
00:04:47,581 --> 00:04:50,416
the vocabulary to articulate
the world around you...

83
00:04:50,584 --> 00:04:53,452
and recognizing the realities
women deal with daily.

84
00:04:53,854 --> 00:04:55,589
That's how I define feminism.

85
00:04:55,590 --> 00:05:00,091
Polar Bear speaks
so clearly and logically...

86
00:05:00,092 --> 00:05:03,162
that I can't imagine
someone like her being blind...

87
00:05:03,163 --> 00:05:04,230
to the challenges women face.

88
00:05:04,866 --> 00:05:08,167
The immediate assumption would be
that a woman voted yes,

89
00:05:08,770 --> 00:05:11,939
so I wondered if she voted
the other way...

90
00:05:11,940 --> 00:05:13,139
just to avoid being pegged like that.

91
00:05:13,140 --> 00:05:14,942
It was just a gut feeling in the moment.

92
00:05:18,312 --> 00:05:19,545
My head is spinning.

93
00:05:20,381 --> 00:05:22,315
- I'm getting a headache.
- Let's just do the dishes.

94
00:05:22,316 --> 00:05:23,116
Sounds good.

95
00:05:23,117 --> 00:05:25,285
I'll wash the glasses and bottles.

96
00:05:25,953 --> 00:05:28,622
Dropping a topic like that
right out of the gate? That's heavy.

97
00:05:28,923 --> 00:05:30,656
- It's intense.
- Tell me about it.

98
00:05:31,392 --> 00:05:33,260
I'll give the perilla leaves
another rinse.

99
00:05:34,628 --> 00:05:37,163
It does make you wonder.

100
00:05:37,164 --> 00:05:39,865
Did people in here really take
such extreme stances?

101
00:05:39,866 --> 00:05:41,602
- Right. Me too.
- That's what I was thinking.

102
00:05:42,103 --> 00:05:43,403
It's pretty overwhelming.

103
00:05:44,305 --> 00:05:46,840
A question like that was bound to trigger
an extreme reaction, though.

104
00:05:47,407 --> 00:05:48,174
The topic itself is...

105
00:05:48,175 --> 00:05:50,844
That controversy was
all over the news back then.

106
00:05:50,845 --> 00:05:53,580
- Right, it was huge.
- People debated that for a long time.

107
00:05:53,881 --> 00:05:56,849
The real issue was
that a government agency...

108
00:05:56,850 --> 00:06:00,353
threw around such an absolute statement
so casually.

109
00:06:05,693 --> 00:06:08,061
That exact line was used
by an actual government body,

110
00:06:08,062 --> 00:06:10,197
the Ministry of Gender Equality
and Family.

111
00:06:10,198 --> 00:06:11,565
So all I said was, "The issue is..."

112
00:06:11,590 --> 00:06:13,800
"that a government institution
published that."

113
00:06:14,134 --> 00:06:16,569
And the room immediately went tense.

114
00:06:16,570 --> 00:06:19,772
I desperately wanted to shout,
"Men aren't perpetrators!"

115
00:06:19,773 --> 00:06:21,907
but holding back was frustrating.

116
00:06:22,743 --> 00:06:24,278
I wanted to debate it
right then and there.

117
00:06:24,945 --> 00:06:26,812
A single unexpected question casts...

118
00:06:26,813 --> 00:06:29,315
a quiet tension over the community.

119
00:06:30,217 --> 00:06:33,486
As night falls,
the Community House shifts...

120
00:06:34,053 --> 00:06:36,555
into an anonymous space.

121
00:06:36,824 --> 00:06:38,424
Starting tonight, every evening,

122
00:06:38,726 --> 00:06:41,227
the residents will conceal
their identities...

123
00:06:41,528 --> 00:06:43,295
and enter heated debates...

124
00:06:43,698 --> 00:06:45,832
behind anonymous screen names...

125
00:06:45,857 --> 00:06:48,267
on gender, politics, class,
and social values.

126
00:06:48,669 --> 00:06:50,803
Tonight's topic is gender.

127
00:06:51,338 --> 00:06:54,607
Will they bridge the divide,
or drift further apart?

128
00:06:56,877 --> 00:06:58,177
(Tension Under the Roof)

129
00:06:58,178 --> 00:07:00,180
(The Community)

130
00:07:00,647 --> 00:07:04,383
(2. A Spy Among Us)

131
00:07:04,819 --> 00:07:09,422
Please stand by
until the anonymous chat opens.

132
00:07:36,984 --> 00:07:39,452
I should've written it down.
My mind just went blank.

133
00:07:43,323 --> 00:07:44,790
(Far Left, Progressive, Conservative)

134
00:07:44,791 --> 00:07:47,327
(Far Left)

135
00:07:49,730 --> 00:07:51,464
(Day 1:
"All men are potential perpetrators.")

136
00:07:51,465 --> 00:07:53,099
(Public Administration major.
Seen him on YouTube.)

137
00:07:57,704 --> 00:08:00,339
(Dark Knight: Suspected Spy,
Offered 1,600 dollars)

138
00:08:00,340 --> 00:08:02,776
There was another
important announcement...

139
00:08:02,777 --> 00:08:05,778
delivered to the residents this morning.

140
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:07,947
(This morning)

141
00:08:07,948 --> 00:08:09,249
How'd you know?

142
00:08:09,495 --> 00:08:10,115
No way!

143
00:08:11,217 --> 00:08:13,519
Here is an additional announcement.

144
00:08:15,456 --> 00:08:17,790
There is a spy among you...

145
00:08:18,025 --> 00:08:21,260
whose mission is to sow discord.

146
00:08:22,897 --> 00:08:24,298
Please proceed with caution.

147
00:08:26,867 --> 00:08:30,436
- So is the spy supposed to be...
- Kind of like an NPC?

148
00:08:30,437 --> 00:08:31,671
Looks like it.

149
00:08:31,972 --> 00:08:33,572
You mean like a hostile NPC?

150
00:08:33,573 --> 00:08:34,540
Not sure.

151
00:08:34,908 --> 00:08:38,862
Maybe someone who sabotages the group
whenever we try to cooperate?

152
00:08:38,886 --> 00:08:40,647
Someone looking to drive wedges
between us.

153
00:08:48,488 --> 00:08:51,191
Polar Bear seems to think
along the same lines as me.

154
00:08:52,726 --> 00:08:54,093
While Michael is...

155
00:08:54,595 --> 00:08:57,463
I bet there are plenty of hidden rules
they haven't told us yet.

156
00:08:57,464 --> 00:08:58,464
Just a personal hunch.

157
00:08:58,465 --> 00:09:00,833
Michael seems to know
an awful lot about this.

158
00:09:00,834 --> 00:09:01,968
Sure you're not the spy?

159
00:09:03,270 --> 00:09:04,403
Just kidding.

160
00:09:04,404 --> 00:09:07,240
If they divide us evenly
down gender lines,

161
00:09:07,908 --> 00:09:09,642
it could spiral into... what's the word?

162
00:09:10,077 --> 00:09:11,510
A full-blown gender war.

163
00:09:11,511 --> 00:09:13,870
Out at the smoking area,
Benjamin came up and brought up...

164
00:09:13,895 --> 00:09:16,349
the whole men-versus-women
divide, didn't he?

165
00:09:16,350 --> 00:09:18,017
Oh yeah. He definitely mentioned that.

166
00:09:27,828 --> 00:09:29,363
Wait, something new just popped up.

167
00:09:29,763 --> 00:09:31,330
Here are the rules...

168
00:09:32,733 --> 00:09:35,668
The anonymous chat will open shortly.

169
00:09:36,403 --> 00:09:39,839
The anonymous chat is held every night.

170
00:09:40,241 --> 00:09:42,675
Every resident must participate...

171
00:09:42,676 --> 00:09:47,213
as an active debater
in two out of the four debates.

172
00:09:47,448 --> 00:09:50,283
Only four? Why just four?

173
00:09:50,684 --> 00:09:53,619
Each day, residents will debate...

174
00:09:53,620 --> 00:09:56,355
a designated topic
in a three-on-three format.

175
00:09:56,690 --> 00:09:58,190
"Residents will debate
a designated topic..."

176
00:09:58,191 --> 00:09:59,191
"in a three-on-three format."

177
00:09:59,559 --> 00:10:03,328
Registration for For and Against is
strictly first-come, first-served,

178
00:10:03,329 --> 00:10:07,666
and anyone not debating
will participate as an observer.

179
00:10:08,201 --> 00:10:09,434
At the end of the debate,

180
00:10:09,703 --> 00:10:12,471
all residents,
both debaters and observers,

181
00:10:12,706 --> 00:10:15,107
will vote on the side
they found more convincing.

182
00:10:16,085 --> 00:10:18,953
This is getting interesting.

183
00:10:18,978 --> 00:10:22,147
Every member of the winning side...

184
00:10:22,148 --> 00:10:25,217
will earn 1,000 dollars in personal funds,

185
00:10:25,419 --> 00:10:27,787
while members of the losing side...

186
00:10:27,788 --> 00:10:30,223
will have 1,000 dollars deducted
from their personal funds.

187
00:10:33,326 --> 00:10:35,894
Regardless of which side they represented,

188
00:10:35,895 --> 00:10:39,198
the single resident voted
as having performed the best...

189
00:10:39,199 --> 00:10:40,966
will be named MVP.

190
00:10:41,468 --> 00:10:45,171
The MVP receives
an additional 1,000-dollar bonus.

191
00:10:45,772 --> 00:10:47,740
In the event of a tie,

192
00:10:48,108 --> 00:10:50,543
the side backed by the MVP
will take the victory.

193
00:10:52,113 --> 00:10:55,915
Registration for today's debate
is now open.

194
00:10:56,550 --> 00:10:59,351
Today's debate category is gender.

195
00:11:00,086 --> 00:11:02,788
The topic is as follows.

196
00:11:03,390 --> 00:11:08,794
"It is only natural to find a man
who pays more on dates attractive."

197
00:11:08,826 --> 00:11:10,030
"Attractive?"

198
00:11:10,463 --> 00:11:14,842
Residents who view this
as instinctive and natural...

199
00:11:14,866 --> 00:11:16,168
should register for For.

200
00:11:16,169 --> 00:11:18,070
Residents who view it...

201
00:11:18,071 --> 00:11:20,974
as a social construct
rather than human nature...

202
00:11:20,975 --> 00:11:23,576
should register for Against.

203
00:11:23,577 --> 00:11:25,278
(It is only natural to find a man
who pays more on dates attractive.)

204
00:11:25,279 --> 00:11:29,115
(Screen names registered
as debate sign-ups begin)

205
00:11:30,417 --> 00:11:32,318
The whole point of an anonymous chat...

206
00:11:32,453 --> 00:11:35,588
is masking who you really are, right?

207
00:11:35,689 --> 00:11:36,956
So I took a gamble.

208
00:11:37,190 --> 00:11:39,224
I figured,
"Let's go completely over the top."

209
00:11:39,626 --> 00:11:41,326
(ID: GCDA)

210
00:11:41,327 --> 00:11:46,665
(GCDA: a well-known feminist slogan)

211
00:11:46,666 --> 00:11:48,100
(Profile Picture)

212
00:11:48,277 --> 00:11:50,311
(Crop)

213
00:11:50,336 --> 00:11:53,539
I almost went with "Girls can do anything"
as my handle,

214
00:11:54,608 --> 00:11:57,200
but then I realized I was steering
straight into a minefield.

215
00:12:00,414 --> 00:12:02,582
"An American guy who knows DC Inside?"

216
00:12:02,917 --> 00:12:05,251
That doesn't really add up, does it?

217
00:12:05,419 --> 00:12:08,121
"An American using four-character idioms?"

218
00:12:08,122 --> 00:12:10,189
Even my Korean American friends
back home...

219
00:12:10,190 --> 00:12:13,326
wouldn't know an expression that obscure.

220
00:12:13,327 --> 00:12:15,162
(A sharp deduction)

221
00:12:15,163 --> 00:12:19,265
Honestly, even I rarely hear
anyone use that in daily conversation.

222
00:12:19,833 --> 00:12:23,702
(DCINSIDE: Michael,
For, "It's natural instinct")

223
00:12:26,073 --> 00:12:29,097
(ID: a1)

224
00:12:29,121 --> 00:12:32,211
I took the first letter of the alphabet
and paired it with the number one...

225
00:12:32,212 --> 00:12:34,114
to give off that "top of the class" vibe.

226
00:12:34,382 --> 00:12:38,017
Plus, when you think of steak,
A.1. is the classic sauce.

227
00:12:38,018 --> 00:12:40,553
And since I'm a huge meat lover,

228
00:12:41,054 --> 00:12:43,989
"a1" just clicked. Short, simple, done.

229
00:12:43,990 --> 00:12:46,992
(a1: Genie, For, "It's natural instinct")

230
00:12:47,727 --> 00:12:49,860
An ID that wouldn't give me away.

231
00:12:50,030 --> 00:12:51,830
I wondered if people would even
recognize the word.

232
00:12:55,135 --> 00:12:58,204
"Totentanz" means "Dance of Death."

233
00:12:58,205 --> 00:12:59,582
I picked it to bring an aura of carnage,

234
00:12:59,607 --> 00:13:02,408
like, "My arguments are going
to tear you all apart."

235
00:13:02,409 --> 00:13:05,645
I wanted that raw intensity,
so I went with "Totentanz."

236
00:13:06,279 --> 00:13:08,447
(Totentanz: Nangja)

237
00:13:08,448 --> 00:13:10,716
(For, "It's natural instinct")

238
00:13:10,717 --> 00:13:12,050
("It is only natural to find a man
who pays more on dates attractive.")

239
00:13:13,520 --> 00:13:14,953
There isn't really a deep story behind it.

240
00:13:14,954 --> 00:13:16,089
I just love strawberries.

241
00:13:17,030 --> 00:13:19,638
(ddalgi: Go Ae Shin,
Against, "It's a social construct")

242
00:13:21,295 --> 00:13:23,696
I panicked at the start...

243
00:13:23,697 --> 00:13:25,164
so I just typed the first thing
that came to mind.

244
00:13:25,999 --> 00:13:28,968
(coco000033: Sugar,
Against, "It's a social construct")

245
00:13:31,138 --> 00:13:34,174
My screen name is karen3000.

246
00:13:34,175 --> 00:13:35,708
No special meaning behind it.

247
00:13:35,709 --> 00:13:38,144
The prompt asked for letters and numbers,
so I just thought,

248
00:13:38,145 --> 00:13:39,779
"Whatever, this works," and hit enter.

249
00:13:39,780 --> 00:13:41,447
(karen3000: Benjamin,
Against, "It's a social construct")

250
00:13:41,448 --> 00:13:43,382
(Against: Benjamin, Go Ae Shin, Sugar)

251
00:13:43,407 --> 00:13:46,543
(For: Genie, Nangja, Michael)

252
00:13:47,621 --> 00:13:49,121
That went fast. Okay.

253
00:13:49,256 --> 00:13:50,489
I ended up sitting this one out.

